au:method_SeedWeight a schema:HowTo,
        skos:Concept,
        appn:Method ;
    dcterms:description "Scanning weight of the seed in g (calculated by mass_correction_factor; mass_correction factor=mean value of actual weight/mean value of seed weight in g from the .csv) (seed weight) using an X-ray CT scanner, at 220kV voltage and 6mA current, utilizing a 0.5mm copper filter for image acquisition at a resolution of 84µm. The specimen stage rotated 220 degrees with a rotation step increment of 0.15 degrees. Throughout the 7-minute scanning duration, 1500 projections were collected at an exposure time of 250 ms each. Correction and reconstruction were carried out using the Fraunhofer EZRT CTProcessingNet, following the approach described by Schmidt et al. (2020) (DOI: 10.1186/s13007-020-00565-w). Reconstructed 3D grey-scale volume, with a depth of 16 bits, was then segmented into 30 individual 3D volumes using the EarSTubesSegmentation algorithm." ;
    dcterms:title "seed weight" ;
    schema:description "Scanning weight of the seed in g (calculated by mass_correction_factor; mass_correction factor=mean value of actual weight/mean value of seed weight in g from the .csv) (seed weight) using an X-ray CT scanner, at 220kV voltage and 6mA current, utilizing a 0.5mm copper filter for image acquisition at a resolution of 84µm. The specimen stage rotated 220 degrees with a rotation step increment of 0.15 degrees. Throughout the 7-minute scanning duration, 1500 projections were collected at an exposure time of 250 ms each. Correction and reconstruction were carried out using the Fraunhofer EZRT CTProcessingNet, following the approach described by Schmidt et al. (2020) (DOI: 10.1186/s13007-020-00565-w). Reconstructed 3D grey-scale volume, with a depth of 16 bits, was then segmented into 30 individual 3D volumes using the EarSTubesSegmentation algorithm." ;
