au:method_SmoothedProjectedShootArea a schema:HowTo,
        skos:Concept,
        appn:Method ;
    dcterms:description "The smoothed projected shoot area (smoothed projected shoot area kpixels) is calculated by smoothing the projected shoot area using splines as described by Brien et al. (2020) (https://doi.org/10.1186/s13007-020-00577-6), employing the R package growthPheno (Brien, 2021c) http://cran.at.r-project.org/package=growthPheno)." ;
    dcterms:title "smoothed projected shoot area" ;
    schema:description "The smoothed projected shoot area (smoothed projected shoot area kpixels) is calculated by smoothing the projected shoot area using splines as described by Brien et al. (2020) (https://doi.org/10.1186/s13007-020-00577-6), employing the R package growthPheno (Brien, 2021c) http://cran.at.r-project.org/package=growthPheno)." ;
    schema:name "smoothed projected shoot area" ;
    skos:inScheme au:cs_Method ;
    skos:prefLabel "smoothed projected shoot area (Method)" .

au:method_SmoothedProjectedShootAreaForASingleTimePoint a schema:HowTo,
        skos:Concept,
        appn:Method ;
    dcterms:description "The smoothed projected shoot area for a single time point is calculated by smoothing the projected shoot area using splines as described by Brien et al. (2020) (https://doi.org/10.1186/s13007-020-00577-6), employing the R package growthPheno (Brien, 2021c) (http://cran.at.r-project.org/package=growthPheno)." ;
    dcterms:title "smoothed projected shoot area for a single time point" ;
    schema:description "The smoothed projected shoot area for a single time point is calculated by smoothing the projected shoot area using splines as described by Brien et al. (2020) (https://doi.org/10.1186/s13007-020-00577-6), employing the R package growthPheno (Brien, 2021c) (http://cran.at.r-project.org/package=growthPheno)." ;
    schema:name "smoothed projected shoot area for a single time point" ;
    skos:inScheme au:cs_Method ;
    skos:prefLabel "smoothed projected shoot area for a single time point (Method)" .

au:method_SpikeCATRadius a schema:HowTo,
        skos:Concept,
        appn:Method ;
    dcterms:description "Scanning spike Circle that has the same Area as the seed maximum Transverse section (CAT) radius calculated using an X-ray CT scanner, at 220kV voltage and 6mA current, utilizing a 0.5mm copper filter for image acquisition at a resolution of 84µm. The specimen stage rotated 220 degrees with a rotation step increment of 0.15 degrees. Throughout the 7-minute scanning duration, 1500 projections were collected at an exposure time of 250 ms each. Correction and reconstruction were carried out using the Fraunhofer EZRT CTProcessingNet, following the approach described by Schmidt et al. (2020). Reconstructed 3D grey-scale volume, with a depth of 16 bits, was then segmented into 30 individual 3D volumes using the EarSTubesSegmentation algorithm. Spike, automatic wheat seed segmentation and measurements were conducted using the EarS algorithm. Spikelet information, including the number of spikelets per spike and the number of grains per spikelet, estimated using a method described by Zhou et al. (2021), with modifications implemented in a Python 3.0 environment." ;
    dcterms:title "spike CAT radius" ;
    schema:description "Scanning spike Circle that has the same Area as the seed maximum Transverse section (CAT) radius calculated using an X-ray CT scanner, at 220kV voltage and 6mA current, utilizing a 0.5mm copper filter for image acquisition at a resolution of 84µm. The specimen stage rotated 220 degrees with a rotation step increment of 0.15 degrees. Throughout the 7-minute scanning duration, 1500 projections were collected at an exposure time of 250 ms each. Correction and reconstruction were carried out using the Fraunhofer EZRT CTProcessingNet, following the approach described by Schmidt et al. (2020). Reconstructed 3D grey-scale volume, with a depth of 16 bits, was then segmented into 30 individual 3D volumes using the EarSTubesSegmentation algorithm. Spike, automatic wheat seed segmentation and measurements were conducted using the EarS algorithm. Spikelet information, including the number of spikelets per spike and the number of grains per spikelet, estimated using a method described by Zhou et al. (2021), with modifications implemented in a Python 3.0 environment." ;
    schema:name "spike CAT radius" ;
    skos:inScheme au:cs_Method ;
    skos:prefLabel "spike CAT radius (Method)" .

au:method_SpikeCATRadiusStandardDeviation a schema:HowTo,
        skos:Concept,
        appn:Method ;
    dcterms:description "Scanning spike Circle that has the same Area as the seed maximum Transverse section (CAT) radius standard deviation calculated using an X-ray CT scanner, at 220kV voltage and 6mA current, utilizing a 0.5mm copper filter for image acquisition at a resolution of 84µm. The specimen stage rotated 220 degrees with a rotation step increment of 0.15 degrees. Throughout the 7-minute scanning duration, 1500 projections were collected at an exposure time of 250 ms each. Correction and reconstruction were carried out using the Fraunhofer EZRT CTProcessingNet, following the approach described by Schmidt et al. (2020). Reconstructed 3D grey-scale volume, with a depth of 16 bits, was then segmented into 30 individual 3D volumes using the EarSTubesSegmentation algorithm. Spike, automatic wheat seed segmentation and measurements were conducted using the EarS algorithm. Spikelet information, including the number of spikelets per spike and the number of grains per spikelet, estimated using a method described by Zhou et al. (2021), with modifications implemented in a Python 3.0 environment." ;
    dcterms:title "spike CAT radius standard deviation" ;
    schema:description "Scanning spike Circle that has the same Area as the seed maximum Transverse section (CAT) radius standard deviation calculated using an X-ray CT scanner, at 220kV voltage and 6mA current, utilizing a 0.5mm copper filter for image acquisition at a resolution of 84µm. The specimen stage rotated 220 degrees with a rotation step increment of 0.15 degrees. Throughout the 7-minute scanning duration, 1500 projections were collected at an exposure time of 250 ms each. Correction and reconstruction were carried out using the Fraunhofer EZRT CTProcessingNet, following the approach described by Schmidt et al. (2020). Reconstructed 3D grey-scale volume, with a depth of 16 bits, was then segmented into 30 individual 3D volumes using the EarSTubesSegmentation algorithm. Spike, automatic wheat seed segmentation and measurements were conducted using the EarS algorithm. Spikelet information, including the number of spikelets per spike and the number of grains per spikelet, estimated using a method described by Zhou et al. (2021), with modifications implemented in a Python 3.0 environment." ;
    schema:name "spike CAT radius standard deviation" ;
    skos:inScheme au:cs_Method ;
    skos:prefLabel "spike CAT radius standard deviation (Method)" .

