au:method_WaterUseIndex a schema:HowTo,
        skos:Concept,
        appn:Method ;
    dcterms:description "Water Use Index (WUI kpixels/mL) was calculated as the ratio of smoothed projected shoot area 50 (proxy for final biomass) to TWU. Higher values of WUI correspond to higher water efficiency (cross-reference traits - smoothed projected shoot area 'smoothed Projected Shoot Area [Trait ID], TWU Total Water Use [Trait ID]), biomass [Trait ID])." ;
    dcterms:title "water use index" ;
    schema:description "Water Use Index (WUI kpixels/mL) was calculated as the ratio of smoothed projected shoot area 50 (proxy for final biomass) to TWU. Higher values of WUI correspond to higher water efficiency (cross-reference traits - smoothed projected shoot area 'smoothed Projected Shoot Area [Trait ID], TWU Total Water Use [Trait ID]), biomass [Trait ID])." ;
